    ABSTRACT: We confirm and extend our previous calculation demonstrating the cancellation (up to two-loop order) of the Glauber multiple scattering corrections (and other similar “long distance” effects) to the Drell-Yan cross section for the process quark + hadron → lepton pair plus anything. Hence these corrections do not violate factorisation. Our calculation is in a light cone axial gauge. An interesting feature of the cancellation is the requirement that the hadronic target be a colour singlet (which is not needed in the analogous calculation in an abelian theory). The cancellation holds whether the target is a meson or a baryon.
